the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(f(x)-5)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1-5\\cdot x\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =1-5(2-0) \\\\  & =1-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114015/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff2f1a9d-2b0e-5a18-98d5-4f49f6f1527b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114015"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346057/field-1/1114f773249b584f03ae90d8348b5b14abd566a3f244c0aad51e974a9460892e" :answer/id #uuid "e15b143b-eafb-5b87-a8dc-4a16ec1aa25e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346057/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "6cf86f9e-790d-5745-857c-1df6f91fc584" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346057/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad9497f7-a6bd-57c1-aaf5-1c8b8e0f4b4a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346057/field-1/1114f773249b584f03ae90d8348b5b14abd566a3f244c0aad51e974a9460892e" :answer-field/choices ["q-346057/field-1/1114f773249b584f03ae90d8348b5b14abd566a3f244c0aad51e974a9460892e" "q-346057/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346057" :question/id #uuid "246ea688-360e-5196-a83d-e47bea5b22da" :question/math-academy-id "q-346057" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3,$ calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(3)\\,+\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6\\,+\\,\\frac{16-1}{2} \\\\  & =6\\,+\\,\\frac{15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346057/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff2f1a9d-2b0e-5a18-98d5-4f49f6f1527b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346057"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114017/selection/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" :answer/id #uuid "9ba58110-7a69-54fb-89f9-c312fd812114" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114017/selection/33ad5bb85ef2860b8848dac07e73b48f485bff167e79bb938240370691781b46" :answer/id #uuid "a119a217-9982-5f31-a9cf-8bc31222630f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "34" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114017/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "232998f1-e760-5ec2-8720-c33cd54e8896" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114017/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "d9b85d4d-4ebf-5914-af45-c1628a1f0799" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114017/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" :answer/id #uuid "67b61998-b20a-51e9-abfd-592ab59c9363" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114017/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4542caf3-f7b1-5790-8f03-00a198fdb357" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114017/selection/33ad5bb85ef2860b8848dac07e73b48f485bff167e79bb938240370691781b46" :answer-field/choices ["q-114017/selection/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" "q-114017/selection/33ad5bb85ef2860b8848dac07e73b48f485bff167e79bb938240370691781b46" "q-114017/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" "q-114017/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-114017/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114017" :question/id #uuid "c1c49f11-39cf-55bf-be78-e57de3366735" :question/math-academy-id "q-114017" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{4}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ calculate\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}(7-5f(x))\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{4}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}(7-5f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =7{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7\\cdot x\\,{|}_{2}^{4}-5\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =7(4-2)+20 \\\\  & =7\\cdot 2+20 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114017/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff2f1a9d-2b0e-5a18-98d5-4f49f6f1527b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114017"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316099/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "4a15426d-b21c-5d7c-a006-f1a1b330dc5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316099/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa0f719c-7b6b-5a4d-903c-6743fff769ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316099/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-316099/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316099" :question/id #uuid "ca667e43-98a3-51cf-8ee3-438b59a6ddfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-316099" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8,$ \nthen what is ${\\int }_{1}^{7}(2-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{7}(2-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{4}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n(-3)+8\\,=\\,{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{7}(2-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{7}1\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,3{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot x{|}_{1}^{7}\\,-\\,3(5) \\\\  & =2(7-1)-15 \\\\  & =12-15 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316099/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316099"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114135/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "b6315a33-9071-54e2-b9ac-3cb3de8f1320" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114135/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "1e342ce5-220b-5b7c-b90f-0a4bad0cedba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114135/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "a7cc3f93-b2e2-55c8-b26f-5f57dbe9c281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114135/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "353ece7b-f1f6-5933-84f3-a3fcd72ef334" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114135/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "13fc8e14-533e-556f-8131-fe3dc0d7a59a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114135/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a693a0d1-75c4-5773-a91c-3015b71b45d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114135/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer-field/choices ["q-114135/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" "q-114135/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-114135/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-114135/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-114135/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114135" :question/id #uuid "4532d7dd-efba-5785-a721-165bfae74c8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114135" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ then what is ${\\int }_{3}^{6}(5-2f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8+4 & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 12 & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{6}(5-2f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\cdot x\\,{|}_{3}^{6}-2\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =5(6-3)-24 \\\\  & =5(3)-24 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114135/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114135"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114133/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "6c60c08f-c067-5560-9388-dcc9cd508b05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114133/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "4d7b50e6-5e79-547f-a4d0-3523fadcd174" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114133/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "73a99681-4e73-57fa-9774-b62220810b0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114133/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "ef942b09-8c13-51a3-8ad0-c6f691e4a472" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114133/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "784b28ce-6ef1-5c7e-98aa-25f80beca79e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114133/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2bc329b-00e9-5c97-812b-73d35b80342e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114133/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-114133/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-114133/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-114133/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-114133/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-114133/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114133" :question/id #uuid "b2b9f164-4690-5b86-8b79-bf8259387b31" :question/math-academy-id "q-114133" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-2$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3,$ then what is ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+3 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 1 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+2\\cdot x\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =1+2(3-0) \\\\  & =1+6 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114133/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114133"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346188/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "cb791b1c-a9ea-52b6-8898-f468d6f30bbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346188/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer/id #uuid "937e73e5-8f69-5b1f-8089-87434d2a8fdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346188/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d118722-2245-5229-9b6b-01a2481dbf7d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346188/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-346188/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-346188/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346188" :question/id #uuid "eec642e8-aa00-5555-b355-9ec662ad96f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-346188" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-5$ then what is ${\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)+4)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)+4)\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n2+(-5)={\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)+4)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{1}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(-3)+4\\cdot x\\,{|}_{1}^{6} \\\\  & =-6+4(6-1) \\\\  & =-6+20 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346188/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346188"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346189/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "dee722b9-9bc9-5851-b8be-fbdcd71df4e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346189/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "65179503-8e8e-558f-82ed-4dd001000cfc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346189/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer-field/choices ["q-346189/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346189" :question/id #uuid "365f9a98-2f82-5cd8-98a6-e5a67719486f" :question/math-academy-id "q-346189" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=7$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ then what is ${\\int }_{0}^{8}(3+f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{8}(3+f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{4}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7+1={\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}(3+f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot x\\,{|}_{0}^{8}+8 \\\\  & =3(8-0)+8 \\\\  & =24+8 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346189/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346189"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114143/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "2b23a4e3-3cfe-5e99-bd3a-33291a12abb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114143/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "d454aabc-56ca-5c64-970a-a6847e824c37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114143/selection/b78cefa051ec62e42babb0396ce415bc1c6b03c29d281d68224ab0312a503d34" :answer/id #uuid "0d1c046d-29e7-576c-bd63-b007a849dacb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114143/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "2dad3368-3b1f-5f30-adb6-5b54b1058bda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114143/selection/c2724874453e84fa99374647d0694dc238ab831bc6b7d897dc21c9d3c7e61851" :answer/id #uuid "b5880e00-93d8-50ca-b06b-d51e42517cef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114143/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c48bd3e-22c1-5da5-929b-92235c89e5ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114143/selection/b78cefa051ec62e42babb0396ce415bc1c6b03c29d281d68224ab0312a503d34" :answer-field/choices ["q-114143/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-114143/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-114143/selection/b78cefa051ec62e42babb0396ce415bc1c6b03c29d281d68224ab0312a503d34" "q-114143/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-114143/selection/c2724874453e84fa99374647d0694dc238ab831bc6b7d897dc21c9d3c7e61851"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114143" :question/id #uuid "700eca56-7546-5c46-a5c9-5b46500fdf20" :question/math-academy-id "q-114143" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{8}^{5}3f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-2$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{3}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{8}^{5}3f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2 \\\\ 3{\\int }_{8}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2 \\\\ -3{\\int }_{5}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2 \\\\ {\\int }_{5}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{5}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114143/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114143"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346226/field-1/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8" :answer/id #uuid "ea337439-3768-513f-830f-a6043d4f5289" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346226/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "54f606cc-6eec-50d2-90c6-fce418e55397" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346226/field-1/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8" :answer-field/choices ["q-346226/field-1/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346226" :question/id #uuid "e93e9065-9494-5342-89db-24beca909847" :question/math-academy-id "q-346226" :question/problem "Let $f$ and $g$ be continuous functions such that ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4,\\,\\,{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{2}{3}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=6,$ and ${\\int }_{-1}^{3}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=-20.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-3}^{-1}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{-1}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{2}{3}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6 \\\\ {\\int }_{-3}^{3}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the adjacent intervals rule and substituting known values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the sum rule for definite integrals,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{-3}^{3}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(-4)-4(9) \\\\  & =-46.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =-46-{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-46-(-20) \\\\  & =-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-346226/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346226"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4790/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "f9fb6bc0-3cf2-5f5c-a0b8-279c58c1c77a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4790/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "9f2b1a05-a696-5bcd-83b1-46477bb4df58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4790/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "de088edb-8704-5be7-a106-c32d7afd6c1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4790/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "4a14cc77-4818-5ce4-a31c-4b7a5e5e26c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4790/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "7b11126c-e054-57bd-9dbc-db1779838a71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4790/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff98cde1-3450-5181-83f4-c8aa84e70126" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4790/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-4790/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-4790/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-4790/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-4790/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-4790/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4790" :question/id #uuid "b49ad214-b312-5d79-8063-a03e0ca82e97" :question/math-academy-id "q-4790" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{3}^{0}\\frac{1}{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=6.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{0}\\frac{1}{3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{3}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3+6 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-4790/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4790"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4796/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "27a01490-a60e-51e2-a28f-fb28b2004451" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4796/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c6095231-508c-5673-bd3c-3f4b3815da10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4796/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "93c1daa6-65f9-5d3b-ad89-6e1227208de9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4796/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "f247bf84-33b6-5c85-b3b3-a4b8ce8abb7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4796/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "c9dd6c17-be8d-52fb-9beb-a964d86a9fa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4796/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4b5f5cc-c453-599b-b999-95893c6bc7d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4796/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-4796/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-4796/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-4796/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-4796/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-4796/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4796" :question/id #uuid "41e5e2a8-7447-512a-b492-6cb29cfa7129" :question/math-academy-id "q-4796" :question/problem "Suppose that $g(x)$ is a  function such that  ${\\int }_{4}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{1}3g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-6.$  What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{1}3g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-6 \\\\ 3{\\int }_{4}^{1}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-6 \\\\ -3{\\int }_{1}^{4}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-6 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{4}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{4}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+5 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-4796/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4796"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346225/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "fa12a659-9565-53af-b941-8827250b633b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346225/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "08ddec81-4b31-587c-8e65-9645ef73232a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346225/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-346225/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346225" :question/id #uuid "18cab19d-8f67-5d6e-9e84-4c7aa4d64f7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-346225" :question/problem "Let $f$ and $g$ be continuous functions such that ${\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=9,\\,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4,$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=10.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-4 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the adjacent intervals rule and substituting known values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the sum rule for definite integrals,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(9)+(-8) \\\\  & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =19-{\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =19-10 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-346225/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346225"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-418"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_\\pi^\\pi \\sqrt{\\sin x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-419"] :question/problem "Given that ${\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{6} \\, f(x) \\; \\textrm d x = -54 },$ what is the value of\n${\\displaystyle \\int_{6}^{0} \\bigg( \\dfrac 1 3 f(x) + 1 \\bigg) \\; \\textrm d x }?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{6}^{0}(\\frac{1}{3}f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{6}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{6}^{0}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 54+x\\,{|}_{6}^{0} \\\\  & =18+(0-6) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-420"] :question/problem "If $\\displaystyle \\int_7^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = 18$ and $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{7}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = -6$ then what is $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{10} \\big( 2f(x)+1 \\big) \\,\\textrm d x?$" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{7}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x + \\displaystyle \\int_7^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = \\displaystyle \\int_0^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6+18={\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 12={\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{10}(2f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{10}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(12)+x\\,{|}_{0}^{10} \\\\  & =24+(10-0) \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-421"] :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\displaystyle \\int_4^1 2 \\, f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = -1}$ \nand ${\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{-1} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 2}.$  What is the value of ${\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^4 f(x) \\, \\textrm dx}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify the first given integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{1}2\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ 2{\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ -2{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second integral can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ -{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ {\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
